  "body": "What happens: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets` (and every `camcraft-ui` lib test build) fails on main `c42eeba78`:\n\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `break_through_from` in initializer of `camcraft_app::operation::OpParams`\n  --> crates/ui/src/height_memo_machine_tests.rs:60:10\n   |\n60 |         &OpParams::Drill {\n```\n\nCause: two PRs that each merged cleanly, but not together.\n- #2504 (merge `90e016a6e`, commit `b50f49a6b`) adds the field `break_through_from` to `OpParams::Drill`.\n- #2498 (merge `c0ae2c578`, commit `30a4ba58c`) adds `crates/ui/src/height_memo_machine_tests.rs`, which builds an `OpParams::Drill` without that field.\n\nGit and the merge planner cannot see this; each PR passed its own gate on the main of its time. Last green on this check: `2f965f7d9`.\n\nFix: add `break_through_from` to the initializer at line 60, with the value that keeps the test's meaning (the default that #2504 gives an existing Drill). Do not change #2504's field.\n\nDone means: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib height_memo_machine` are green on main.\n",
